{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1427483585,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg3MDYxNDcz","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/89#issuecomment-87061473"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\n\u003e atm I setup a symlink under bin/ which immediately reminded that on windows it\n\u003e wouldn't work, so I would need copies of the shim scripts\n\u003e \n\u003e windows can run .py scripts (https://docs.python.org/2/faq/windows.html#id3).\n\u003e It probably also could run \"normal way\" in a shell (provided by git?) any\n\u003e script with correct (which would be what?) shebang... since we probably\n\u003e wouldn't want to ask people adjust PATHEXT env, I guess we will just end up\n\u003e with .bat scripts to call into our scripts (which would or would not have .py)\n\u003e \n\u003e does annex uses git's shell while running external remotes, @joeyh?\n\ngit-annex generally does not use the shell.\n\nIf datalad is running at the console, .BAT files are probably the way to\ngo. If you want datalad to run without a console window, you will have\nto use .VBS launcher files or a similar hack.\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1427485540,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg3MDY4ODAz","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/89#issuecomment-87068803"},"message":".VBS -- didn't hear about them from my 15 years ago experience... THANKS!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1427491956,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg3MDk3NjU1","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/89#issuecomment-87097655"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\n\u003e .VBS -- didn't hear about them from my 15 years ago experience... THANKS!\n\nYou can find an example of them in the git-annex windows build.\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1427518809,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg3MTYwNzAx","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/89#issuecomment-87160701"},"message":"just for a memory substitute, here is relevant code from within Build/NullSoftInstaller.hs\n\n``` haskell\n        webappscript \u003c- vbsLauncher tmpdir \"git-annex-webapp\" \"git-annex webapp\"\n        autostartscript \u003c- vbsLauncher tmpdir \"git-annex-autostart\" \"git annex assistant --autostart\"\n...\nvbsLauncher :: FilePath -\u003e String -\u003e String -\u003e IO String\nvbsLauncher tmpdir basename cmd = do\n    let f = tmpdir \u003c/\u003e basename ++ \".vbs\"\n    writeFile f $ unlines\n        [ \"Set objshell=CreateObject(\\\"Wscript.Shell\\\")\"\n        , \"objShell.Run(\\\"\" ++ cmd ++ \"\\\"), 0, False\"\n        ]\n    return f\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1427531331,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg3MTkwMjI1","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/89#issuecomment-87190225"},"message":"Why not just using the \"Git Bash\"? We know it's available, it makes things\nmore similiar to linux, so why ignore it? I somehow miss the point here.\n\n2015-03-28 6:00 GMT+01:00 Yaroslav Halchenko notifications@github.com:\n\n\u003e just for a memory substitute, here is relevant code from within\n\u003e Build/NullSoftInstaller.hs\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e     webappscript \u003c- vbsLauncher tmpdir \"git-annex-webapp\" \"git-annex webapp\"\n\u003e     autostartscript \u003c- vbsLauncher tmpdir \"git-annex-autostart\" \"git annex assistant --autostart\"\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ...vbsLauncher :: FilePath -\u003e String -\u003e String -\u003e IO String\n\u003e vbsLauncher tmpdir basename cmd = do\n\u003e     let f = tmpdir \u003c/\u003e basename ++ \".vbs\"\n\u003e     writeFile f $